    <!-- Notification reading. -->
    <string name="notif_listen_title">Read notifications</string>
    <string name="notif_listen_body">Your work calendar lives inside Outlook and Teams, which never sync to the phone\'s calendar — so the only way Medha can see a work meeting is the notification those apps post.\n\nAndroid has one switch for this and it covers every notification on the phone; there is no way to limit it to some apps. So Medha filters instead, on the device, and keeps nothing: notification text is never written to storage. It either becomes a brief line that expires in 8 hours, or it is discarded.\n\nAnything that looks like a passcode is dropped before anything else happens, with no exceptions. A one-time code on your home screen would defeat the point of sending it.</string>
    <string name="notif_listen_grant">Open Android settings</string>
